1
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:23,750
Floating on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,840
aiming for that day,

3
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:31,438
when I kicked a pebble,

4
00:00:31,488 --> 00:00:34,000
my shoes flew off too,

5
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:39,810
snipping along the way,

6
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:42,220
onto the carpenter's head,

7
00:00:42,220 --> 00:00:45,914
if I stayed a kid,

8
00:00:45,964 --> 00:00:48,460
I got laughed at.

9
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:55,260
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,
it's all for nothing.

10
00:00:55,260 --> 00:01:02,560
even yawns go unused,
the streetscape is strangely gentle.

11
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:14,620
from the pointed hat's water flask,
up to the vast heavens.

12
00:01:14,620 --> 00:01:16,780
the sun sets,

13
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:25,260
tomorrow too, it'll end just like this

14
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:29,040
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness again, they say.

15
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:31,760
Only after losing it did I realize,

16
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:33,860
because I'm such a fool.

17
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:41,920
Rookie Detective Ryotsu

18
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:48,380
Good morning.

19
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:51,060
Good morning, sir.

20
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:53,880
That's right.
Today's the big cleaning, isn't it?

21
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:55,220
Yes, it is.

22
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:58,700
But Ryo-chan showed up and
then disappeared somewhere.

23
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:01,780
He's really hopeless.

24
00:02:01,780 --> 00:02:03,900
When he gets back,
I'll give him a stern scolding.

25
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:05,840
Alright, let's clean, let's clean!

26
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:07,320
I'll help too.

27
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:07,840
Yes.

28
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:22,040
Are you all right, Terai-san?

29
00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:23,820
I'm fine.

30
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:28,240
This is...

31
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,280
This looks like a very old photo, though.

32
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:35,400
This is the history of
this Kōen-mae police box.

33
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:38,120
These are photos of the
officers who served here.

34
00:02:38,660 --> 00:02:41,360
This is a photo from when I first came here.

35
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:44,680
So young!
So you had a time like this too, Chief.

36
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:46,420
Of course.

37
00:02:46,420 --> 00:02:49,020
Nobody becomes chief overnight, you know.

38
00:02:49,020 --> 00:02:53,580
By the way, this is Chief Iwata,
who was in charge here back then.

39
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:57,600
He was gentle and sincere,
a true model of a police officer.

40
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:01,980
Could this be...

41
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:05,080
There's only one person
who'd pull a stunt this stupid.

42
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:06,640
Ryo-chan, as expected?

43
00:03:07,660 --> 00:03:11,020
He was assigned straight to this
police box right after graduating.

44
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:14,860
Actually, I met Ryotsu the
day before he was assigned here.

45
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:16,480
Really?

46
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:21,020
We got a report that a
drunk was going wild downtown.

47
00:03:24,380 --> 00:03:26,340
Hey! Settle down!

48
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:29,340
Think I'd be drinking if
I were scared of the cops?

49
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:30,400
What?

50
00:03:34,340 --> 00:03:36,240
Cool your head there overnight!

51
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:38,460
That guy was Ryotsu.

52
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:43,340
When I learned he was the officer being
assigned to the Kameari Park police box,

53
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:45,260
I was sent to pick him up.

54
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:49,280
Thank you for coming to meet me.

55
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:51,520
How could such a ridiculous thing happen?

56
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:53,300
Now, now, calm down.

57
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:54,920
It's an old story.

58
00:03:55,640 --> 00:03:59,820
On top of that, I ended up being
made the trainer of the new recruits.

59
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:02,040
Whenever we went on patrol together,

60
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:04,280
Ah.

61
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:06,800
He always disappears.

62
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:10,240
Hehe, big haul, big haul!

63
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:11,440
Hey, Ryotsu!

64
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:12,700
Or perhaps

65
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:15,780
Loan!

66
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:17,540
Yay!

67
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:18,920
Hey, Ryotsu!

68
00:04:19,380 --> 00:04:20,440
Or else

69
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:24,160
Alright! Number three! Number three! Go! Go!

70
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,220
Hey, Ryotsu!

71
00:04:27,180 --> 00:04:30,220
By rights, he should have been
fired right then and there.

72
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:31,760
But Chief Iwata

73
00:04:32,420 --> 00:04:33,680
He's still young.

74
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:37,820
Someone who trains people
mustn't lose their temper.

75
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:40,500
Come on, come on.

76
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:45,000
There was even a time I patrolled with
him on a leash so he wouldn't run off.

77
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:47,120
Ow ow

78
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:50,320
My shoes hurt because I'm
not used to wearing them.

79
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:52,640
Thank you very much.

80
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:58,700
In the end,
I had to buy him sandals with my own money.

81
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:03,140
The sandals he's wearing now
are the ones from that time.

82
00:05:03,940 --> 00:05:06,380
That long ago? They're antiques.

83
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:09,320
So you've been a senior officer since way back,
haven't you?

84
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:14,360
Ryo-san isn't wearing
his uniform in this one.

85
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:15,520
That's unusual.

86
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:21,180
This is a photo taken when Ryotsu was assigned
to the criminal investigation division.

87
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:22,120
Criminal investigation division?

88
00:05:22,380 --> 00:05:24,320
So you were a detective, senpai?

89
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:27,300
But it was only for a short time.

90
00:05:27,980 --> 00:05:29,520
I've never heard that before.

91
00:05:30,900 --> 00:05:35,240
He's got a memory or two he
can't bring himself to talk about.

92
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:37,900
Jan-jan-jaan!

93
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:39,720
Jan-jan-jaan!

94
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:42,600
Baan-baan!

95
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:43,680
Got it!

96
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:46,480
Ryotsu,
what have you been doing this whole time?

97
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:47,380
Huh?

98
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:50,460
Senpai,
you didn't watch Yuhi ni Iru, did you?

99
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:53,460
I only watch the news
and period dramas on TV.

100
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:56,920
That's a waste, it's such a fun show.

101
00:05:58,280 --> 00:06:00,840
Senpai,
how does one become a detective, anyway?

102
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:03,100
After all, once you've joined the police,

103
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:04,960
don't you want to try being a detective?

104
00:06:06,380 --> 00:06:06,903
Detective?

105
00:06:06,953 --> 00:06:10,540
Someone who can't even handle police
box duty can't possibly be a detective!

106
00:06:10,540 --> 00:06:13,360
I'm just not cut out for police box duty,
you know.

107
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:17,520
Nothing big ever happens,
and I have to wear these uncool uniforms.

108
00:06:17,940 --> 00:06:20,840
Of course it's better
when no incidents happen!

109
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:32,220
Right, if you caught ten wanted criminals, the
criminal investigation division might call you up.

110
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:33,820
Well, that's impossible, though.

111
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:35,060
I see.

112
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:37,020
Stop!

113
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:40,960
You thieving bastard!

114
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:46,960
Damn it! Not this story!

115
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:48,560
I'd rather die than talk!

116
00:06:53,740 --> 00:06:55,040
Instant win!

117
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:09,080
Stop! You're under arrest!

118
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:15,480
What? Ryotsu's going to be a detective?

119
00:07:15,880 --> 00:07:18,460
The criminal investigation
chief insisted on it, so...

120
00:07:18,460 --> 00:07:22,040
But he's short-tempered,
short-legged, and simple-minded.

121
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:24,020
His only redeeming quality
is his physical strength.

122
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:25,500
That's apparently what they liked about him.

123
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:28,420
Let's send him off with a smile, shall we?

124
00:07:29,340 --> 00:07:30,340
Y-yes, sir.

125
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:37,060
So this is my battlefield from today on.

126
00:07:38,260 --> 00:07:39,500
Boss, coming in!

127
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:48,500
Who are you?

128
00:07:48,660 --> 00:07:52,420
It's Ryotsu. Kankichi Ryotsu.
I became a detective today.

129
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:53,800
Ryotsu?

130
00:07:55,060 --> 00:07:56,100
Oh, right.

131
00:07:57,380 --> 00:08:01,040
Hey, everyone. This is Ryotsu, who's been
assigned to this section starting today.

132
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:02,960
Please call me Jeans.

133
00:08:03,860 --> 00:08:05,680
What, you're a half-breed?

134
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:07,080
It's a nickname.

135
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:09,720
Detectives usually call each other by nicknames,
don't they?

136
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:11,520
Well, we don't do that here.

137
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:14,320
Then please start doing that from now on.

138
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:17,620
By the way,
from now on I'll be wearing jeans every day.

139
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:19,780
So, Jeans Detective!

140
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:22,980
The Jeans from First Chome...

141
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:26,100
Hey, somebody lend him some pants.

142
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:30,620
What are those baggy things?

143
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:34,720
With those, he's a pants detective.

144
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:36,980
Don't laugh so much, okay?

145
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:38,800
Just call me Ryotsu, already.

146
00:08:38,800 --> 00:08:40,500
Well, don't get so angry.

147
00:08:40,920 --> 00:08:43,800
Nanbu, here, I'm leaving the rest to you.

148
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:47,060
I'm Nanbu, your new partner.

149
00:08:47,420 --> 00:08:49,000
Nice to meet you, Dekapan Deka.

150
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,380
I said it's Ryotsu!

151
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:00,240
What's that?

152
00:09:01,060 --> 00:09:04,460
Yūhi ni Hoero, the one where detectives
go around town questioning people.

153
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:08,320
What is this "Yūhi ni Hoero" thing?

154
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:12,200
It's a detective drama on TV.

155
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:14,240
You haven't watched it?
And you're a detective?

156
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:16,360
Unfortunately,
I haven't had the time to watch it.

157
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:19,080
Is that drama really that good?

158
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:20,240
It's outstanding.

159
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:22,560
The ending of Jeans Detective was amazing,
wasn't it?

160
00:09:23,660 --> 00:09:24,560
What on earth is this?!

161
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:29,460
What are you doing, Nanbu-san?

162
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:32,060
Look at that.

163
00:09:38,760 --> 00:09:39,400
Akimoto!

164
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:41,700
Ryotsu!

165
00:09:42,660 --> 00:09:43,400
Let's go!

166
00:09:43,860 --> 00:09:44,200
Yes!

167
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:50,640
Hey!

168
00:09:52,060 --> 00:09:53,180
What do you think you're doing?

169
00:09:53,180 --> 00:09:53,860
Damn it!

170
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:56,260
Ryotsu, he went your way!

171
00:09:56,900 --> 00:09:57,700
I won't let him get away!

172
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:30,520
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeh...
no, no, no!

173
00:10:30,980 --> 00:10:31,840
Are you done yet? Yes!

174
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:36,540
Hey, hey,
what's with that way of putting it on?

175
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:39,360
The way to put it on is,
you know, properly...

176
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:47,400
Yo, Ohara, you did your best

177
00:10:47,660 --> 00:10:49,880
Ryotsu, what are you doing here?

178
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:52,480
I just stopped by on my way
back from the investigation.

179
00:10:52,740 --> 00:10:55,012
Hey, hey, you know what?

180
00:10:55,062 --> 00:10:57,820
I'm the one who caught this phantom thief,
you know.

181
00:10:58,060 --> 00:10:59,080
So I heard.

182
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:04,960
Arresting three people, so I really
was cut out to be a detective after all.

183
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:06,064
Well,

184
00:11:06,114 --> 00:11:10,380
Ohara, you also worked as the
hands and feet of us detectives.

185
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:12,500
Well then, I'm dismissing you for now.

186
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:17,100
That idiot, getting so full of himself.

187
00:11:33,780 --> 00:11:35,920
Hey, Ryotsu,
we're going to canvass the area.

188
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:40,180
Again? Can't we do some
interrogations for a change?

189
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:43,440
Once the suspect we're chasing is caught,
alright, let's go.

190
00:11:58,100 --> 00:11:58,798
Nanbu-san,

191
00:11:58,848 --> 00:12:02,140
Isn't there no suspect left around here?

192
00:12:03,780 --> 00:12:04,600
But it's pointless.

193
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:09,140
But what if the suspect
shows up after we've given up?

194
00:12:09,140 --> 00:12:09,620
But...

195
00:12:11,780 --> 00:12:15,100
If this were a detective drama,
we'd find a lead right away.

196
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:23,360
I see.

197
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:25,220
Yeah, yeah.

198
00:12:26,020 --> 00:12:26,660
Understood.

199
00:12:27,260 --> 00:12:27,580
Well then,

200
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:31,020
What happened?

201
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:35,300
Apparently the suspect we were
chasing was caught in Kyushu.

202
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:38,900
So everything we've
been doing was pointless?

203
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:41,940
Don't sulk about it.
It happens all the time.

204
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:45,040
Anyway, on to the next job.
Come on, cheer up.

205
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:45,740
Yes.

206
00:12:54,140 --> 00:12:57,960
Nanbu-san, how long do we
have to keep dressed like this?

207
00:12:58,400 --> 00:13:00,540
Until we find out what
the Ōtaguro gang is up to.

208
00:13:01,380 --> 00:13:03,500
Lately those guys have become quite active.

209
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:06,520
Maybe they're in the
middle of some big deal.

210
00:13:07,520 --> 00:13:09,020
But if nothing happens,

211
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:11,720
then that's a happy ending, isn't it.

212
00:13:13,260 --> 00:13:16,400
I really don't want anyone we
know to see us dressed like this.

213
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:20,040
What's wrong?

214
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:20,820
Look, look.

215
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:23,160
Someone you know?

216
00:13:23,620 --> 00:13:25,140
A senior from the transmission station.

217
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:30,020
Out soaking up the sun again today,
are you, grandpa?

218
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:32,780
It's the policeman.

219
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:34,380
What beautiful weather we're having today.

220
00:13:34,780 --> 00:13:35,140
Yes.

221
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:39,380
Ryotsu, Japan is said to be
a country with little crime.

222
00:13:39,980 --> 00:13:41,200
Do you know why that is?

223
00:13:42,800 --> 00:13:45,060
I don't know.

224
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:49,320
It's because there are
police boxes all over town,

225
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:52,460
and police officers patrol like that.

226
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,340
What happened?

227
00:14:08,340 --> 00:14:10,560
This case is bigger than we imagined.

228
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:16,220
The boss of the Ōtaguro gang,
who was on the run abroad, has returned.

229
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:19,420
He's wanted on charges
of gambling and murder.

230
00:14:19,420 --> 00:14:22,480
Let's go. We'll take the back door.

231
00:14:22,480 --> 00:14:22,760
Yes.

232
00:14:24,180 --> 00:14:25,920
You're finally starting
to look like a detective.

233
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:27,380
Count on you, Ryotsu.

234
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:28,420
Leave it to me.

235
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:38,360
Ōtaguro.

236
00:14:38,360 --> 00:14:39,460
Good night.

237
00:14:39,460 --> 00:14:39,920
Hurry.

238
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:40,920
Chase him!

239
00:14:40,920 --> 00:14:41,180
Yes.

240
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:44,940
Get back here!

241
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:55,760
Ryotsu-kun?

242
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:58,580
It's Ryotsu-kun after all!

243
00:14:58,580 --> 00:14:59,600
No way, it really is him.

244
00:15:00,340 --> 00:15:01,800
What's with that getup?

245
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:03,700
Didn't you become a police officer?

246
00:15:03,700 --> 00:15:04,820
Have you turned into a suspicious character?

247
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:07,440
Ōtaguro!

248
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:11,800
Damn it!

249
00:15:14,900 --> 00:15:15,920
You idiot!

250
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:22,600
You let the suspect get away because
you ran into a middle school classmate?

251
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:24,260
That's no excuse!

252
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:26,320
But...

253
00:15:27,060 --> 00:15:27,820
You...

254
00:15:27,820 --> 00:15:30,320
That's enough.

255
00:15:35,940 --> 00:15:39,440
Tch, Nanbu, you didn't have to hit him.

256
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:44,320
Ryo, you know what Ōtaguro
is charged with, right?

257
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:45,200
Yeah.

258
00:15:46,640 --> 00:15:49,260
Gambling and murder, right?

259
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:53,360
The person Ōtaguro killed
was Nanbu's fiancée.

260
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:53,780
What?

261
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:57,640
But Nanbu never said a word about that.

262
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:02,080
He probably figured telling you
would just put extra pressure on you.

263
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:07,380
That cheerful Nanbu had a past like that...

264
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:09,840
That's just how detectives are.

265
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:19,100
Nanbu-san

266
00:16:19,860 --> 00:16:20,220
Yeah.

267
00:16:23,880 --> 00:16:25,020
It's you.

268
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:27,920
I'm sorry.

269
00:16:29,420 --> 00:16:31,640
I didn't even understand how you felt,
Nanbu-san.

270
00:16:32,080 --> 00:16:34,540
Always just putting on airs and showing off,

271
00:16:34,590 --> 00:16:37,100
I'm, I'm, I'm a worthless guy!

272
00:16:38,160 --> 00:16:39,680
Don't get so down, Ryotsu.

273
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:44,097
I lost my temper too, and

274
00:16:44,147 --> 00:16:45,560
I'm sorry I hit you.

275
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:46,780
No way!

276
00:16:47,700 --> 00:16:49,315
Alright, let's pull ourselves together,

277
00:16:49,365 --> 00:16:51,800
and this time,
let's arrest Ōtaguro together!

278
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:54,640
Yes!

279
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:03,360
Nan-san, I bought it.

280
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:04,420
Thanks for your hard work.

281
00:17:07,820 --> 00:17:09,100
It's been a week, you know.

282
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:12,520
Isn't Ōtaguro already gone, fled abroad?

283
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:14,720
Could be.

284
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:17,040
Then isn't staying here a waste of time?

285
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:20,080
But he's got his money hidden here.

286
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:23,680
There's a chance he'll come to
get it before fleeing the country.

287
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:25,380
Let's wait a little longer.

288
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:29,580
Still, I'd like a proper
meal once in a while.

289
00:17:30,020 --> 00:17:31,220
Don't be so down about it.

290
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:34,100
Once this case is solved,
I'll take you out for drinks.

291
00:17:34,100 --> 00:17:35,020
Really?

292
00:17:35,020 --> 00:17:38,340
That's right, you're not of age yet.

293
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:40,900
My twentieth birthday is this March 3rd.

294
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:42,720
Alright, then it's a promise.

295
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:45,300
On the 3rd, let's drink until morning.

296
00:17:45,300 --> 00:17:45,980
Yay!

297
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:53,380
That's his car.

298
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:57,300
Ryotsu, go call for backup right away.

299
00:17:57,300 --> 00:17:57,720
Yes.

300
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:08,600
Oh no, I don't have a 10-yen coin!

301
00:18:10,180 --> 00:18:12,280
Hey you, hand over your money.

302
00:18:12,280 --> 00:18:15,140
Just hurry up and give me your money.

303
00:18:15,140 --> 00:18:18,380
Officer, officer!

304
00:18:18,380 --> 00:18:21,048
Come on, hurry, hurry.

305
00:18:21,098 --> 00:18:24,120
I said hand over the money.

306
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:27,700
Hey, Ryo-su, what are you doing?

307
00:18:27,700 --> 00:18:28,732
S-senior!

308
00:18:28,782 --> 00:18:31,709
The culprit showed up over there,
but I don't have a 10-yen coin,

309
00:18:31,759 --> 00:18:34,060
if I don't hurry, he might get away!

310
00:18:34,180 --> 00:18:34,560
What!?

311
00:18:36,300 --> 00:18:40,360
You idiot!
You can call 110 without a ten-yen coin!

312
00:18:40,420 --> 00:18:41,380
Is that right!

313
00:18:41,880 --> 00:18:44,420
I'll contact the station!
You go back to the scene!

314
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:45,000
Y-yes, sir!

315
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:53,100
Damn, he's already come out...

316
00:19:00,540 --> 00:19:01,180
Hurry!

317
00:19:01,740 --> 00:19:04,120
Ōtaguro, you're not getting away!

318
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:05,820
Get him!

319
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:07,940
Don't let him do it!

320
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:17,600
Ōtaguro,
you're under arrest for gambling and murder!

321
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:19,580
Nanbu-san!

322
00:19:19,820 --> 00:19:22,300
Ryotsu!
Don't let the others get away either!

323
00:19:24,040 --> 00:19:24,660
Bastards!

324
00:19:57,780 --> 00:19:58,980
But, but, but!

325
00:19:59,780 --> 00:20:01,580
You're a detective too, you know!

326
00:20:03,080 --> 00:20:05,580
We've got to catch him, no matter what!

327
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:19,040
Hup, cut him off!

328
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:38,100
Aaaaaah!

329
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:39,520
Aaaaaah!

330
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:41,300
Aaaaaah!

331
00:20:41,300 --> 00:20:43,460
Aaaaaah!

332
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:47,420
Ōtaguro!

333
00:20:47,420 --> 00:20:50,140
Shake him off!

334
00:20:50,140 --> 00:20:51,360
Go that way!

335
00:20:51,360 --> 00:20:52,960
Aaaaaah!

336
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:54,600
Aaaaaah!

337
00:20:54,600 --> 00:21:00,300
Ow!

338
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:21,760
Nooooooooooooooooooooooo... no, no, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no!

339
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:28,700
Aaaaaah!
You shot the Love Star, you bastard!

340
00:21:29,180 --> 00:21:30,280
Clatter, clatter!

341
00:21:41,780 --> 00:21:45,220
Senpai, four...

342
00:21:46,740 --> 00:21:47,820
Nanbu-san was

343
00:21:52,640 --> 00:21:53,680
no good.

344
00:21:54,540 --> 00:21:55,420
N-no way.

345
00:21:56,920 --> 00:21:57,360
That can't be.

346
00:21:59,380 --> 00:22:03,240
If only I'd called for
backup a little sooner.

347
00:22:08,260 --> 00:22:10,060
Is that drama any good?

348
00:22:10,060 --> 00:22:15,100
Come on, cheer up.

349
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:20,820
Let's drink until morning tonight.

350
00:22:24,980 --> 00:22:26,980
You're a detective too, you know!

351
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:32,660
Nanbu-san.

352
00:22:40,700 --> 00:22:42,700
A while later...

353
00:22:46,140 --> 00:22:47,920
Good morning.

354
00:22:48,580 --> 00:22:50,580
Ryotsu? What are you doing here?

355
00:22:51,540 --> 00:22:54,140
I realized I didn't
understand anything at all.

356
00:22:55,660 --> 00:22:58,380
Please, let me work here again.

357
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,100
Ryotsu.

358
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:12,860
And that's how he came back here.

359
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:18,080
Though he soon went back to being the usual Ryotsu,
of course.

360
00:23:19,020 --> 00:23:22,060
So Ryo-chan has had a hard time too

361
00:23:24,320 --> 00:23:26,060
So, could today be

362
00:23:27,860 --> 00:23:28,620
I see.

363
00:23:32,840 --> 00:23:35,660
Nam-san, the weather was just like this that day too,
wasn't it.

364
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:41,600
As for me,
I'm still being an idiot as always.

365
00:23:42,860 --> 00:23:45,380
I'm nowhere near becoming like Nanbu-san.

366
00:23:49,320 --> 00:23:52,540
Drinks are on me today.
Let's drink until we drop!

367
00:24:15,380 --> 00:24:23,700
Surprise and commotion, with spirit and resolve,
solving things quickly, and helping out!

368
00:24:23,700 --> 00:24:35,280
That's the way it goes, with flashes of inspiration,
bouncing along, gathering everything, taking action, and soaring away!

369
00:24:36,320 --> 00:24:39,900
Above all, Smoy Power!

370
00:24:40,220 --> 00:24:46,040
Gather everyone, if you come here,

371
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:52,280
the dreamlike, final energy.

372
00:24:53,280 --> 00:24:56,720
Gaze at tomorrow, believe in yesterday,

373
00:24:56,720 --> 00:24:59,620
paint the universe,
and if you stand on the earth,

374
00:24:59,620 --> 00:25:03,420
the star of Kameari spins
around and draws a circle.

375
00:25:05,760 --> 00:25:07,060
This should be fine, right?

376
00:25:07,060 --> 00:25:08,560
Like hell it is!

